<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Intentionally minimal.

    No components are declared yet: there is no UI code, no provider, and no
    worker. Declaring an activity or a DocumentsProvider here before the class
    exists would produce a manifest that references something the build cannot
    resolve, and an app that appears to have a launcher it cannot start.

    The namespace lives in app/build.gradle.kts, not here (AGP 8 requirement).
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
        Permissions are deliberately absent.

        Every permission requested must be justified against a shipping feature
        and recorded in the V-02 scope matrix (PRD.md 8, Rules.md 23). Requesting
        a permission no feature uses is a Play Store policy violation and a
        consent-screen lie, so the manifest starts empty and grows only when a
        feature that needs one exists.

        When they are added, note that none of them may be justified as
        "improves performance" - the storage permissions will be for SAF tree
        access only, and the app requests no storage permission for its own use,
        because it stores no file content (Rules.md 2).
    -->

</manifest>
